Add --separate-lora to gRPCServerCLI

LoRA deltas merge into the model weights at load unless the base is quantized,
bf16 or JIT-offloaded, and a merged-LoRA load bypasses the weights cache in
both directions, so an f16 base plus a LoRA re-reads the full checkpoint from
disk on every generation. The app-side settings ModelPreloader subscribes to
are unreachable from the server, which builds an empty settings workspace in a
fresh temp dir every boot. The flag sets ModelZoo.isSeparateLoRAPreferred,
read at the top of isQuantizedModel, which is the single function all fourteen
decision sites reach. LoHa still merges, since there is no separate path for
it.
